atement":"DeleteSpaceMember is the declared handler entry and begins by obtaining the current user.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"other-principal-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler binds the current user and caller membership while resolving the requested space member resource.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":742,"endLine":748}]},{"id":"other-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"Resource resolution binds the target user and active target membership in the caller's space before the authorization decision.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"other-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The handler identifies the target as not self; under the supplied scenario premise this is the different-member relation.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":750,"endLine":751}]},{"id":"other-control","kind":"control","statement":"For a non-self target, the strongest visible authorization control requires the caller's membership to be a space administrator; failure returns an error.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":751,"endLine":755},{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":54,"endLine":59}]},{"id":"other-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"The membership deletion call occurs only after the non-self administrator check and is therefore not reached on this path.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":756,"endLine":763}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]},{"obligationId":"scenario%3Aself-leave::entry%3Adelete-space-member-handler","decision":{"kind":"observed","observed":"allow"},"branchResults":[],"explanation":"At the declared DeleteSpaceMember entry, the handler requires the current authenticated user, resolves the caller and target memberships, and compares their user IDs. Because the accepted premise says the target is the caller's own active membership, isSelf is true, so the non-self administrator check is skipped. The handler then proceeds to the Store.DeleteSpaceMember call, making the source-visible authorization result allow for self-leave. Separately, the accepted policy allows an active member to delete their own membership to leave, so the observed source behavior matches the policy result. The source proves authorization to reach the protected effect, but does not establish whether the external store operation ultimately succeeds; that execution/deployment fact is outside this declared authorization boundary and is not decisive to the handler's authorization branch.","facts":[{"id":"self-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"DeleteSpaceMember is the declared handler entry and obtains the current user before resolving the target membership.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"self-principal-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler binds the current user and caller membership through current-user authentication and resource resolution.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":742,"endLine":748}]},{"id":"self-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"Resource resolution binds the target user and active target membership in the selected space.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"self-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The handler tests whether the target user ID equals the current user ID; under the supplied scenario premise this condition is true.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":750,"endLine":750}]},{"id":"self-control","kind":"control","statement":"The administrator check is conditional on a non-self target, so it does not apply when the target is the caller.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-66ca8138a5e00794","startLine":751,"endLine":755}]},{"id":"self-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"After 